{{also|takeback}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|take<,,took,taken> back}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[retract]] or [[withdraw]] (an [[earlier]] [[statement]]).
#: {{syn|en|recant|unsay|Thesaurus:recant}}
#: {{ux|en|No, you are not fat; I '''take''' it all '''back'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cause]] (someone) to [[remember]] some [[past]] [[event]] or [[time]].
#: {{ux|en|That tune '''takes''' me '''back''' to my childhood.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[resume]] a [[relationship]] with (someone).
#: {{ux|en|She has forgiven him, and '''taken''' him '''back'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[regain]] [[possession]] of (something).
#: {{ux|en|The wedding is off, and he has '''taken back''' the ring.}}
# {{senseid|en|refund}}{{lb|en|transitive}} To [[return]] (something) to a vendor for a refund.
#: {{ux|en|'''Take back''' faulty goods to the shop where you bought them.}}

